KZ3 patch 1149 (SPU pass 139): the runtime's timed condition-variable waits on ps3_evcv (patch 1148), off ntdll's futex queue.
Credit: the Killzone 2 port, patches 6042-6044 (the same conversion on its tree; the sites here are our own list).
Converted (type, init, wake and wait): lv2s_mutex (lv2_sync_core.h: the live sys_lwmutex/lwcond/mutex/cond core, patch 1122), the
sys_event queue (sys_event_queue_receive incl. EVT_RECV_KICK, sys_timer's push) and event flag, the lv2_register SPU-port bind wait,
spu_channels ch_wait_cv (10 ms), spu_workload WAIT_SIGNAL (1 s), cellSpurs event-flag wait, cellSync2 cond/queue waits, the sysPrxForUser lwcond
HLE, kz3_lwcond_fifo.h. Untimed callers of the same cv types (sys_event INFINITE waits) move with their type; sys_cond's unused cv stays.
Not converted: spurs_kern_sched.h's kz3_kwake (patch 1143: events under Wine; its SRW branch runs on native Windows only, where the race does not
exist), cellFiber and spu_lockstep (INFINITE waits on their own cv; no timeout, no alert left behind), rsx_live_draw.c (three INFINITE waits,
in a renderer patch, not changed here).
Behaviour on a quiet system is unchanged (same predicates and timeouts); PS3_CV_STATS=1 prints waits/woken/timeouts/late per wait site, which
replaces patch 1144's guess of the exposure by a count of the wakes that met a timeout.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (group B, R&C 2026-11-09): spu_ch_wake keeps #619/#626's pass through ch_wait_lock (6bea2d59,
the lost-wakeup fix) before ps3_evcv_wake_all: ps3_evcv links a waiter only after its predicate test under ch_wait_lock, so
it does not order the wake by itself. v0.19's new SYS_EVENT_QUEUE_DESTROY_FORCE path (#621/#622) wakes not_empty with
ps3_evcv_wake_all (it called WakeAllConditionVariable on what is a ps3_evcv here). sys_event_queue_receive's timed wait is
upstream's deadline loop (see 1144).

